# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never commit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
# The placeholder template IS committed. Note: a trailing comment on a pattern
# line does NOT work in gitignore -- `#` only starts a comment at the start of
# a line, so it would silently become part of the pattern and match nothing.
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# Compose reads this automatically when present. It is where local ports and
# credentials end up, so it must never be committed -- unlike the base
# docker-compose.yml, which is.
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yaml

# Database dumps. Loading a benchmark or snapshotting local state produces
# these, and they contain real data.
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.sql.bz2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project-specific: things that are large, regenerable, or licensed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Benchmark data. Spider and BIRD are CC BY-SA 4.0 and are deliberately NOT
# vendored — a download script fetches them. See docs/ml/DATASETS.md §7.
#
# Two things under data/ ARE committed, and both are reproducibility records
# rather than data: the digests of the archives every recorded number was
# computed from, and the database-level split assignment. A split that is
# regenerated instead of read makes two runs incomparable (EVALUATION.md §2).
# Note the pattern is `data/*` and not `data/` — git will not descend into an
# ignored *directory*, so a later negation could never re-include anything.
data/*
!data/artifacts.lock.json
!data/splits/
data/splits/*
!data/splits/*.json
!data/splits/*.jsonl
datasets/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Model checkpoints. Large, and derivative works of CC BY-SA data.
# See docs/ml/TRAINING.md §10.
checkpoints/
models/
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.ckpt

# Eval harness output. Per-question artifacts are large and regenerable;
# the *numbers* live in docs/ml/BENCHMARKS.md, which IS committed.
results/
runs/
outputs/
.benchmarks/

# Raw embedding arrays, if ever written to disk rather than to pgvector.
*.npy
*.npz

# Local Postgres volume if bind-mounted by docker compose
pgdata/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/

build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.dmypy.json
.hypothesis/

.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
coverage.json
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs and profiling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
*.prof
locust_report*.html

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notebooks
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Agent/editor tooling: shared project settings would be committed, but the
# .local variants hold machine-specific paths and permissions.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Merge and patch leftovers -- committing these is always a mistake.
*.orig
*.rej

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   docs/assets/     architecture + ER diagrams belong in version control
#   .env.example     placeholder template
#   requirements*.txt pinned deps are the reproducibility record
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
